---
import BaseLayout from '../components/BaseLayout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';

const githubUrl = import.meta.env.PUBLIC_GITHUB_URL ?? 'https://github.com/udiram/VoxelWeave-Designer';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Documentation"
  description="VoxelWeave Designer documentation: the six-workspace workflow, source and output contracts, and research-use boundaries."
  active="documentation"
>
  <div class="content-page">
    <section class="section-shell">
      <div class="page-intro">
        <h1>Documentation for an inspectable fabrication workflow.</h1>
        <p>VoxelWeave Designer keeps source geometry, calibration identity, tool ownership, emitted paths, and scan-back evidence connected inside a saved <code>.voxelweave</code> project.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="content-grid">
        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Six workspaces</h2>
          <p>The desktop workspace is organized around the decisions that change a physical run.</p>
          <ol>
            <li><strong>Design</strong> — create primitives, import solids, transform geometry, and define material regions.</li>
            <li><strong>DICOM</strong> — import a complete series and inspect synchronized axial, sagittal, coronal, and 3D views.</li>
            <li><strong>Calibrate</strong> — bind tool, material, scanner, reconstruction, and rail-width-to-HU evidence.</li>
            <li><strong>Prepare</strong> — audit exact toolpaths, clipping, flow, bed, runtime, and safety checks.</li>
            <li><strong>Send</strong> — export a local, inspectable run package. Printing remains attended and external.</li>
            <li><strong>Verify</strong> — register scan-back data, compare HU, preserve provenance, and export a research package.</li>
          </ol>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Source contract</h2>
          <p>Full-resolution signed HU data in the scientific engine is the source of truth. Display pyramids and WebGL textures are previews only.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>DICOM geometry follows physical patient coordinates and orientation matrices, not filename order or screenshots.</li>
            <li>Complete-series import is required for volume-aware output.</li>
            <li>Continuous-volume output samples the selected physical slab at printer-layer centers without artificial slice interfaces.</li>
            <li>Tile output preserves source-plane identity and keeps structural labels outside the calibrated measurement region.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Output contract</h2>
          <p>The conversion path is explicit and auditable:</p>
          <table class="contract-table">
            <thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage</th><th scope="col">Contract</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Calibrate</td><td>Commanded rail width maps monotonically to measured HU for the bound tool/material/scanner context.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Convert</td><td>Selected source values become fixed-pitch, alternating X/Y variable-width roads.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Audit</td><td>Generated G-code is reverse-audited with manifests, transforms, hashes, and a toolpath trace.</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Verify</td><td>Scan-back comparison remains a separate evidence step; a successful export is not physical proof.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Saved run package</h2>
          <p>A run package is intended for collaboration and review, not only for printer transfer.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Project document and source-series identity.</li>
            <li>Calibration identity, tool/material ownership, and locked print parameters.</li>
            <li>Source-to-print transforms, generated G-code, manifests, and file hashes.</li>
            <li>Toolpath trace, audit findings, and any explicit acknowledgments.</li>
            <li>Scan-back registration, comparisons, plots, and research conclusions when available.</li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>What v1 does not do</h2>
          <p>VoxelWeave Designer v1 does not provide diagnostic interpretation, automatic anatomical segmentation, oblique printing, curved planar reformations, STEP/B-rep CAD, automatic printer start, silent calibration extrapolation, or scientific conversion from preview data.</p>
          <a class="text-link" href="/scientific-boundary/">Read the scientific boundary <Icon name="arrow" size={18} /></a>
        </article>

        <article class="content-block">
          <h2>Source and license</h2>
          <p>The public release, issue history, reproducibility materials, and license are maintained with the source repository.</p>
          <a class="button-secondary" href={githubUrl} target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open the GitHub repository <Icon name="external" size={16} /></a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
